From 514a83a80715828e6c0126417f5681c8080d96c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loop-uh <loop-uh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:40:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Accept client sockets handed over by the node's 443
 dispatcher

When the node sets XRAY_VPNBOT_HANDOFF_DIR, every raw-TCP inbound that
listens on an IPv4 loopback address keeps its TCP listener and also
takes client sockets on <dir>/<port>.handoff: a SOCK_SEQPACKET socket
whose messages carry TCP sockets passed with SCM_RIGHTS by the node's
443 dispatcher (vpnbot node-services go/cmd/sni-dispatch). The
dispatcher peeks the ClientHello without consuming it, picks the inbound
by SNI and hands over the client socket itself, so the inbound reads the
untouched ClientHello, sees the real client address and no proxy stays
in the data path.

Both listeners feed the same TLS/REALITY handling and handler. The TCP
listener is exactly as configured, so local probes and the dispatcher's
copy path keep reaching the inbound there, and its PROXY wrapper never
sees a handed-over socket: there is no proxy in front of one, so there
is no header. Anything received that is not a TCP socket is closed; a
full backlog holds the sender (backpressure); Close ends both and frees
the path. Without the directory nothing changes.

Capability marker: vpnbot-socket-handoff-v2 (v1 meant a listen path
ending in .handoff instead of TCP; no node used it).
